11. Role-Based Access Control

You'll often hear:

RBAC — Role-Based Access Control

It means permissions can be associated with roles.

For example:

Admin
 ├── manage users
 ├── manage products
 ├── manage suppliers
 └── view reports

Manager
 ├── manage products
 ├── manage suppliers
 └── view reports

Storekeeper
 ├── view products
 ├── record purchases
 └── record sales

Then instead of checking every person's name:

Is Megersa allowed?

we can reason:

What role does Megersa have?
        ↓
    Storekeeper
        ↓
What permissions does Storekeeper have?
